  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "slam target to origin tile or slam adjacent area, stunning",
    "skill1": "gain shield, then interrupt and disarm an enemy",
    "skill2": "cleanse own debuffs and reduce damage taken briefly",
    "skill3": "battle max HP increase",
    "skill4": "remain steadfast; gain shield for each ally behind",
    "skill5": "recover HP when casting cleanse skill"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Lucca]] gains a shield, then **interrupts and disarms** an enemy while cleansing her own debuffs for brief **damage reduction**. Her ultimate slams a target to origin or **stuns adjacent tiles** when they cannot be returned. She stays Steadfast and stacks **shields for each ally behind** her in formation. Cleansing also **recovers HP**, and battle max HP grows over time for durability. She is a **durable disruptor** for packed frontlines that need control. **Disarm-immune foes** or enemies that never cluster for the slam see limited control value. Her cleanse skill also recovers HP when used, giving her a self-sustain loop between disruption casts on the frontline. Steadfast status protects her while stacking shields behind allies.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Lucca]] is a **frontline disruptor** — **interrupts and disarms**, self-cleanses, and stays **Steadfast** while stacking **shields from allies behind**. The **fast Quake Slam** stuns clustered tiles or returns a target to origin, so packed lines feed that control. You **cannot displace** [[Lucca]] — cut through the shields with true-damage melee like [[Himmel]] or [[Zorya]], and cancel the slam window with [[Lily May]]. Keep spacing so the adjacent stun and return slam waste themselves."
}
